{{!--
  PRELOADER v2
  Sequence:
  1. "prem design" letter-by-letter reveal (left to right)
  2. Dot falls from top, bounces between words
  3. Words reverse out (right to left stagger)
  4. Dot fades out; particle system fades in as globe
  5. Globe surface ripples (1.2s), then bursts outward (0.5s)
  6. Preloader fades out, hero entrance triggers
--}}

<style>
  .preloader-wordmark {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: clamp(calc(3rem * var(--type-scale-heading, 1)), calc(15vw * var(--type-scale-heading, 1)), calc(12rem * var(--type-scale-heading, 1)));
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .preloader-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(calc(0.875rem * var(--type-scale-body, 1)), calc(2vw * var(--type-scale-body, 1)), calc(1.125rem * var(--type-scale-body, 1)));
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: preloaderSubtitleReveal 0.6s ease-out 2.5s both;
  }

  @keyframes preloaderSubtitleReveal {
    from { opacity: 0; }
    to { opacity: 1; }
  }
</style>

<section id="preloader" class="preloader">
  {{!-- Indeterminate — no aria-valuenow on purpose (WAI-ARIA: omit it when
        the duration isn't known, same reason the visible % text was
        dropped; see main.css's .preloader-progress-bar comment). ONE
        streak (.progress-bar-streak) — was a Material Design two-bar
        chase, reverted 2026-08-06 ("too many firing off": two overlapping
        bars × two duplicate layers below = 4 visible streaks) — see
        main.css's comment on .progress-bar-streak/bar-comet-shoot for the
        current "comet/shooting star" motion design. .progress-bar-streak and
        the .progress-bar-track marker are SHARED with .scroll-progress
        (default.hbs) — same animated-bar system reused for page-to-page
        navigation, not a preloader-only component (see page-transition.js).
        The streak is duplicated TWICE — once in .progress-bar-clip (crisp,
        clipped to the track), once in .progress-bar-glow (identical,
        blurred, stacked on top) — see main.css's comment on those two
        classes for why a real duplicate layer, not box-shadow, and why it
        has to live outside the clip. --}}
  <div class="preloader-progress-bar progress-bar-track" id="preloader-progress-bar" role="progressbar" aria-valuetext="Loading" aria-label="Loading">
    <div class="progress-bar-clip">
      <div class="progress-bar-streak"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="progress-bar-glow" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="progress-bar-streak"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="preloader-content">
    <div class="preloader-wordmark" data-skip-animation="true">
      <span class="pl-word-prem serif">prems</span><span class="preloader-dot sans">.</span><span class="pl-word-design sans">design</span>
    </div>
    <!--<h2 class="preloader-subtitle" id="preloader-subtitle">Product Designer</h2>-->
  </div>
</section>
